1. MyLaneIo.cpp:526: the engine reads PLC rows through MyLaneIO.IOInputBit, whose golden cap 0x300..0x303 answered `true` for SnAllSafeDoor at 0x310 -- the all-doors bit made by 73824bd was never seen (always "closed"). Model 1 (SafePlcModel=1) now accepts 0x300..0x310 (same line); model 0 stays golden.
2. InitialSafeDoor: JerryYang 20260926's temporary "safe doors not ready" MARK (cinitial.cpp:3044-3050) and SAFE_DOOR_AMOUNT=1 (:3083-3084) run after the PLC force-enable (:2792-2797), so every PLC door read IsOff()==false and MES1611+ never fired. New cinitial.cpp EOF W906_SafeDoorPlcEnable, called on the last line of InitialSafeDoor, re-enables (Type 1) only the iSafeDoor[] doors the IO table puts on the PLC (ISABase 4), only with SafePlcIO=1 and SafePlcModel=1; every other door / configuration keeps the MARK.

tests/test_myplc_modbus.cpp [6] goes through the engine's path (MyLaneIO.IOInputBit, Sen.Enable): 69/69 (the [5] check used TMyPLC_IO_Modbus::IsOn, a different path, which is why it was green). Flow9050_Tray 104/104. Debug + release (affected targets). WORKLOG section 2 row 141.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
